{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_srqbiioq6urvnjnobs24edeoyi3jssonomeimbvthfrtade3krlq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. The Rust translation of `rgb_to_hsv` is behaviourally identical to the C.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **SYMBOLS.md** — C exports exactly one symbol (`rgb_to_hsv`); Rust exports it. Symbol diff empty; all undefined symbols are libc/unwind runtime imports. Parity is asserted by `run_tests.sh`, not just by hand.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 30 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass (randomized, fixed-seed, plus exhaustive grids). 31 tests.\n- [x] **Binary stdout** — N/A; neither project builds an executable (`add_library SHARED` / `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` only).\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 16 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, plus generic FFI boundaries. 22 tests.\n- [x] **Feature combos** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, so default is the only combination; run under both dev and release profiles.\n\n## Three real problems found and fixed\n\n1. **The harness was silently vacuous.** `cargo test` does *not* rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target, so tests were dlopening a stale `.so`. I proved it by mutating `src/lib.rs` and watching the suite still pass. Fixed with `assert_so_is_fresh()` in both test files plus `run_tests.sh`, which builds the cdylib and injects its path.\n\n2. **Aliasing rows had a blind spot.** Rows 26–29 drove overlapping `dest`/`src` with random *chromatic* values only, so the `delta == 0 || max == 0` early-out was never exercised under aliasing — a mistranslation that re-reads `src` after writing `dest` needs both conditions simultaneously. Caught by mutation testing; rows now fold in `early_out_triples()` (black, signed-zero black, positive/negative/`FLT_MIN` grey, `max == 0 && delta != 0`).\n\n3. **A genuine NULL-pointer divergence, correctly scoped.** C dies with `SIGSEGV`(11); the dev-profile Rust `.so` dies with `SIGABRT`(6) because `-C debug-assertions=on` emits a null-deref UB check ahead of the raw store. Release matches C exactly. Documented in `ERRORS.md`; `err12b` asserts \"both die by fatal signal\" always, and identical signal under `not(debug_assertions)`.\n\n## Confidence: mutation-tested harness\n\n`mutation_check.sh` injects 34 plausible mistranslations. **28/28 behaviour-changing mutants killed.** The 6 survivors are *provably* observationally equivalent, each with a proof in-script — I verified these rather than assuming they were blind spots:\n\n- `c_min` with `<=`: differs only for `{+0.0, −0.0}`, and every such case is swallowed by the early-out before `delta` is observable.\n- Hue branch reordering (two variants): branches can only disagree on a max-tie, where the formulae coincide *exactly* — if `r == g == max` then `b == min`, so `delta/delta == 1` and `2 + (−delta)/delta == 1`.\n- `delta` and `s` widened to `f64`: Figueroa's theorem — double rounding is innocuous for a single op when `53 ≥ 2·24 + 2`. Widening a *chain* is **not** equivalent (the C rounds intermediate `g − b` to f32), and those mutants are killed.\n- `rem_euclid(360)`: `|g−b| ≤ delta` bounds `h` to `[−60, 300] ∪ {NaN}`, so it can never overflow and `rem_euclid` performs the identical `h + 360.0`.\n\nThat last group matters for interpretation: branch order and single-op precision are *not* observable in this algorithm, so the C's unusual-looking `if/else if` ordering carries no behavioural requirement — only the per-branch formulae do.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified (`git status` clean). Run `./run_tests.sh` for the full matrix, `./mutation_check.sh` to re-validate the suite's sharpness."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":123583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":908,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio